const hanumanChalisa = <ChalisaVerse>[
  ChalisaVerse(number: 1, type: 'doha', native: 'श्रीगुरु चरन सरोज रज, निज मन मुकुर सुधारि।\nबरनउँ रघुबर बिमल जसु, जो दायक फल चारि', transliteration: 'Shri guru charan saroj raj, nij man mukur sudhari / Barnau Raghubar bimal jasu, jo dayak phal chari', meaning: 'Cleansing the mirror of my mind with the dust of my Guru\'s lotus feet, I sing the pure glory of Rama, which bestows the four fruits of life.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 2, type: 'doha', native: 'बुद्धिहीन तनु जानिके, सुमिरौं पवन-कुमार।\nबल बुद्धि विद्या देहु मोहिं, हरहु कलेस विकार', transliteration: 'Buddhiheen tanu jaanike, sumirau Pavan-kumar / Bal buddhi vidya dehu mohi, harahu kales vikar', meaning: 'Knowing myself to be without wisdom, I remember you, son of the Wind. Grant me strength, intelligence, and knowledge, and take away my sorrows and faults.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 3, type: 'chaupai', native: 'जय हनुमान ज्ञान गुण सागर।\nजय कपीस तिहुँ लोक उजागर', transliteration: 'Jai Hanuman gyan gun sagar / Jai Kapis tihu lok ujagar', meaning: 'Victory to Hanuman, ocean of wisdom and virtue! Victory to the Lord of the monkeys, who lights up the three worlds.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 4, type: 'chaupai', native: 'राम दूत अतुलित बल धामा।\nअंजनि-पुत्र पवनसुत नामा', transliteration: 'Ram doot atulit bal dhama / Anjani-putra Pavansut nama', meaning: 'You are Rama\'s messenger, the abode of matchless strength, known as the son of Anjana and the son of the Wind.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 5, type: 'chaupai', native: 'महाबीर बिक्रम बजरंगी।\nकुमति निवार सुमति के संगी', transliteration: 'Mahabir bikram bajrangi / Kumati nivar sumati ke sangi', meaning: 'Great hero, mighty and strong as a thunderbolt; you drive away bad thoughts and befriend good sense.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 6, type: 'chaupai', native: 'कंचन बरन बिराज सुबेसा।\nकानन कुण्डल कुँचित केसा', transliteration: 'Kanchan baran biraj subesa / Kanan kundal kunchit kesa', meaning: 'Golden-hued and beautifully adorned, with rings in your ears and curly hair.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 7, type: 'chaupai', native: 'हाथ बज्र औ ध्वजा बिराजै।\nकॉंधे मूँज जनेऊ साजै', transliteration: 'Hath bajra au dhwaja biraje / Kandhe moonj janeu saje', meaning: 'In your hands shine the thunderbolt-mace and a banner; a sacred thread of munja grass graces your shoulder.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 8, type: 'chaupai', native: 'शंकर सुवन केसरी नंदन।\nतेज प्रताप महा जग बंदन', transliteration: 'Shankar suvan Kesari nandan / Tej pratap maha jag bandan', meaning: 'Offspring of Shiva and joy of Kesari; your radiance and glory are honored by the whole world.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 9, type: 'chaupai', native: 'विद्यावान गुणी अति चातुर।\nराम काज करिबे को आतुर', transliteration: 'Vidyavan guni ati chatur / Ram kaj karibe ko atur', meaning: 'Learned, virtuous, and exceedingly clever, ever eager to do Rama\'s work.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 10, type: 'chaupai', native: 'प्रभु चरित्र सुनिबे को रसिया।\nराम लखन सीता मन बसिया', transliteration: 'Prabhu charitra sunibe ko rasiya / Ram Lakhan Sita man basiya', meaning: 'You delight in hearing the Lord\'s deeds; Rama, Lakshmana, and Sita dwell within your heart.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 11, type: 'chaupai', native: 'सूक्ष्म रूप धरि सियहिं दिखावा।\nबिकट रूप धरि लंक जरावा', transliteration: 'Sukshma roop dhari Siyahi dikhava / Bikat roop dhari Lank jarava', meaning: 'Taking a tiny form, you appeared before Sita; taking a fearsome form, you burned Lanka.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 12, type: 'chaupai', native: 'भीम रूप धरि असुर सँहारे।\nरामचंद्र के काज सँवारे', transliteration: 'Bhim roop dhari asur sanhare / Ramchandra ke kaj savare', meaning: 'Assuming a mighty form, you destroyed the demons and accomplished Rama\'s tasks.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 13, type: 'chaupai', native: 'लाय सजीवन लखन जियाये।\nश्रीरघुबीर हरषि उर लाये', transliteration: 'Laye Sanjivan Lakhan jiyaye / Shri Raghubir harashi ur laye', meaning: 'You brought the Sanjivani herb and revived Lakshmana; overjoyed, Rama held you to his heart.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 14, type: 'chaupai', native: 'रघुपति कीन्ही बहुत बड़ाई।\nतुम मम प्रिय भरतहि सम भाई', transliteration: 'Raghupati kinhi bahut badai / Tum mam priya Bharat-hi sam bhai', meaning: 'Rama praised you greatly, saying: you are as dear to me as my own brother Bharata.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 15, type: 'chaupai', native: 'सहस बदन तुम्हरो यश गावैं।\nअस कहि श्रीपति कंठ लगावैं', transliteration: 'Sahas badan tumharo jas gave / As kahi Shripati kanth lagave', meaning: 'May the thousand-mouthed serpent sing your glory; saying so, the Lord embraced you.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 16, type: 'chaupai', native: 'सनकादिक ब्रह्मादि मुनीसा।\nनारद सारद सहित अहीसा', transliteration: 'Sanakadik Brahmadi muneesa / Narad Sarad sahit Aheesa', meaning: 'The sages like Sanaka, Brahma and the great seers, Narada, Saraswati, and the serpent-king,'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 17, type: 'chaupai', native: 'यम कुबेर दिगपाल जहाँ ते।\nकवि कोविद कहि सके कहाँ ते', transliteration: 'Jam Kuber Digpal jahan te / Kavi kovid kahi sake kahan te', meaning: 'Yama, Kubera, and the guardians of the directions; even poets and scholars cannot fully tell your glory.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 18, type: 'chaupai', native: 'तुम उपकार सुग्रीवहिं कीन्हा।\nराम मिलाय राज पद दीन्हा', transliteration: 'Tum upkar Sugreevahi keenha / Ram milaye rajpad deenha', meaning: 'You did Sugriva a great kindness, uniting him with Rama and winning him his kingdom.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 19, type: 'chaupai', native: 'तुम्हरो मंत्र बिभीषन माना।\nलंकेस्वर भये सब जग जाना', transliteration: 'Tumharo mantra Vibheeshan mana / Lankeshwar bhaye sab jag jana', meaning: 'Vibhishana heeded your counsel and became lord of Lanka, as all the world knows.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 20, type: 'chaupai', native: 'जुग सहस्र योजन पर भानू।\nलील्यो ताहि मधुर फल जानू', transliteration: 'Jug sahasra jojan par Bhanu / Leelyo tahi madhur phal janu', meaning: 'Though the sun is thousands of leagues away, you leapt toward it, taking it for a sweet fruit.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 21, type: 'chaupai', native: 'प्रभु मुद्रिका मेलि मुख माहीं।\nजलधि लाँघि गये अचरज नाहीं', transliteration: 'Prabhu mudrika meli mukh mahi / Jaladhi langhi gaye achraj nahi', meaning: 'Carrying the Lord\'s ring in your mouth, you leapt across the ocean; no wonder in that.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 22, type: 'chaupai', native: 'दुर्गम काज जगत के जेते।\nसुगम अनुग्रह तुम्हरे तेते', transliteration: 'Durgam kaj jagat ke jete / Sugam anugraha tumhare tete', meaning: 'All the hardest tasks in the world become easy by your grace.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 23, type: 'chaupai', native: 'राम दुआरे तुम रखवारे।\nहोत न आज्ञा बिनु पैसारे', transliteration: 'Ram duware tum rakhvare / Hot na aagya binu paisare', meaning: 'You are the guardian at Rama\'s door; none may enter without your leave.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 24, type: 'chaupai', native: 'सब सुख लहै तुम्हारी सरना।\nतुम रक्षक काहू को डरना', transliteration: 'Sab sukh lahai tumhari sarna / Tum rakshak kahu ko darna', meaning: 'All happiness is found in your shelter; with you as protector, there is nothing to fear.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 25, type: 'chaupai', native: 'आपन तेज सम्हारो आपै।\nतीनों लोक हाँक तै काँपै', transliteration: 'Aapan tej samharo aapai / Teenon lok hank te kaanpai', meaning: 'You alone can hold back your own might; at your roar the three worlds tremble.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 26, type: 'chaupai', native: 'भूत पिसाच निकट नहिं आवै।\nमहावीर जब नाम सुनावै', transliteration: 'Bhoot pisach nikat nahi aavai / Mahabir jab naam sunavai', meaning: 'Ghosts and evil spirits dare not come near wherever the great hero\'s name is uttered.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 27, type: 'chaupai', native: 'नासै रोग हरै सब पीरा।\nजपत निरंतर हनुमत बीरा', transliteration: 'Nase rog harai sab peera / Japat nirantar Hanumat beera', meaning: 'Diseases vanish and all pain is removed by ceaselessly repeating the name of brave Hanuman.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 28, type: 'chaupai', native: 'संकट ते हनुमान छुड़ावै।\nमन क्रम बचन ध्यान जो लावै', transliteration: 'Sankat te Hanuman chhudavai / Man kram bachan dhyan jo lavai', meaning: 'Hanuman frees from every trouble those who hold him in thought, deed, and word.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 29, type: 'chaupai', native: 'सब पर राम तपस्वी राजा।\nतिनके काज सकल तुम साजा', transliteration: 'Sab par Ram tapasvi raja / Tin ke kaj sakal tum saja', meaning: 'Rama, the ascetic king, reigns over all; and you carry out all his work.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 30, type: 'chaupai', native: 'और मनोरथ जो कोई लावै।\nसोइ अमित जीवन फल पावै', transliteration: 'Aur manorath jo koi lavai / Soi amit jeevan phal pavai', meaning: 'Whoever brings any heartfelt wish to you gains its fruit, abundant and lasting.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 31, type: 'chaupai', native: 'चारों जुग परताप तुम्हारा।\nहै परसिद्ध जगत उजियारा', transliteration: 'Charon jug partap tumhara / Hai parsiddh jagat ujiyara', meaning: 'Your glory shines through all four ages; your fame lights up the whole world.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 32, type: 'chaupai', native: 'साधु संत के तुम रखवारे।\nअसुर निकंदन राम दुलारे', transliteration: 'Sadhu sant ke tum rakhvare / Asur nikandan Ram dulare', meaning: 'You are the guardian of saints and sages, the destroyer of demons, beloved of Rama.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 33, type: 'chaupai', native: 'अष्ट सिद्धि नौ निधि के दाता।\nअस बर दीन जानकी माता', transliteration: 'Ashta siddhi nau nidhi ke data / As bar deen Janki mata', meaning: 'You bestow the eight powers and nine treasures; this boon was granted to you by Mother Sita.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 34, type: 'chaupai', native: 'राम रसायन तुम्हरे पासा।\nसदा रहो रघुपति के दासा', transliteration: 'Ram rasayan tumhare pasa / Sada raho Raghupati ke dasa', meaning: 'You hold the elixir of devotion to Rama; may you ever remain the servant of Rama.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 35, type: 'chaupai', native: 'तुम्हरे भजन राम को पावै।\nजनम जनम के दुख बिसरावै', transliteration: 'Tumhare bhajan Ram ko pavai / Janam janam ke dukh bisravai', meaning: 'Through singing your praise one reaches Rama, and the sorrows of many births are washed away.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 36, type: 'chaupai', native: 'अन्त काल रघुबर पुर जाई।\nजहाँ जन्म हरि-भक्त कहाई', transliteration: 'Ant kaal Raghubar pur jai / Jahan janam Hari-bhakt kahai', meaning: 'At life\'s end one goes to Rama\'s abode, and is thereafter born a devotee of the Lord.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 37, type: 'chaupai', native: 'और देवता चित्त न धरई।\nहनुमत सेइ सर्व सुख करई', transliteration: 'Aur devta chitt na dharai / Hanumat sei sarva sukh karai', meaning: 'One need hold no other god in mind; serving Hanuman brings every happiness.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 38, type: 'chaupai', native: 'संकट कटै मिटै सब पीरा।\nजो सुमिरै हनुमत बलबीरा', transliteration: 'Sankat katai mitai sab peera / Jo sumirai Hanumat balbeera', meaning: 'All troubles are cut away and every pain removed for whoever remembers the mighty Hanuman.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 39, type: 'chaupai', native: 'जै जै जै हनुमान गोसाईं।\nकृपा करहु गुरुदेव की नाईं', transliteration: 'Jai Jai Jai Hanuman Gosai / Kripa karahu Gurudev ki nai', meaning: 'Victory, victory, victory to Lord Hanuman! Bestow your grace on me as my own divine Guru.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 40, type: 'chaupai', native: 'जो सत बार पाठ कर कोई।\nछूटहिं बंदि महासुख होई', transliteration: 'Jo sat bar path kar koi / Chhutahi bandi maha sukh hoi', meaning: 'Whoever recites this a hundred times is freed from bondage and gains great joy.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 41, type: 'chaupai', native: 'जो यह पढ़ै हनुमान चालीसा।\nहोय सिद्धि साखी गौरीसा', transliteration: 'Jo yah padhai Hanuman Chalisa / Hoy siddhi sakhi Gaurisa', meaning: 'Whoever reads this Hanuman Chalisa attains success; Shiva himself stands witness.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 42, type: 'chaupai', native: 'तुलसीदास सदा हरि चेरा।\nकीजै नाथ हृदय महँ डेरा', transliteration: 'Tulsidas sada Hari chera / Keejai nath hriday mah dera', meaning: 'Tulsidas is ever the servant of the Lord; O master, make your home forever in my heart.'),
  ChalisaVerse(number: 43, type: 'doha', native: 'पवन तनय संकट हरन, मंगल मूरति रूप।\nरामलखन सीता सहित, हृदय बसहु सुर भूप', transliteration: 'Pavan tanay sankat haran, mangal murati roop / Ram Lakhan Sita sahit, hriday basahu sur bhoop', meaning: 'O son of the Wind, remover of troubles, embodiment of all that is auspicious: dwell in my heart together with Rama, Lakshmana, and Sita, O king of gods.'),
];
